{title: 507 - Moment by Moment}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #507 • MOMENT BY MOMENT • 9.10.10.10}
{lyricist: Daniel W. Whittle}
{composer: Mary Whittle}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 507}
{meta: tune MOMENT BY MOMENT}
{meta: meter 9.10.10.10}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Dying with Jesus, [Dm/A]by [C7/Bb]death reckoned [F/C]mine,
[F/C]Living with [Gbm/Db]Jesus, [Gm/D]a new life [Dm]divine,
[Gm/D]Looking [F/C]to Jesus [C7/Bb]till glory [Am]doth [C7/Bb]shine,
[F/C]Moment by [C7/Bb]moment, [Dm/A]O Lord, I [Dbm/Ab]am Thine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Dbm/Ab]Moment [Gm]by moment [Dm/A]I'm kept [C7/Bb]in His [F/C]love;
[F/C]Moment by moment [Bb]I've life from above;
[Abm]Looking to Jesus [Am]till glory doth shine;
[Am]Moment [Gm]by [F]moment, [Gm]O Lord, I [C/G]am [F/C]Thine.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]Never a [Dm/A]trial that [C7/Bb]He is [F/C]not there,
[F/C]Never a [Gbm/Db]burden [Gm/D]that He doth [Dm]not bear,
[Gm/D]Never [F/C]a sorrow [C7/Bb]that He [Am]doth not [C7/Bb]share,
[F/C]Moment by [C7/Bb]moment [Dm/A]I'm under [Dbm/Ab]His care.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]Never a [Dm/A]heart-ache, [C7/Bb]and never [F/C]a groan,
[F/C]Never a [Gbm/Db]teardrop [Gm/D]and never [Dm]a moan;
[Gm/D]Never [F/C]a danger [C7/Bb]but there [Am]on teh [C7/Bb]throne,
[F/C]Moment by [C7/Bb]moment [Dm/A]He thinks of [Dbm/Ab]His own.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Am]Never a [Dm/A]weakness [C7/Bb]that He doth [F/C]not feel,
[F/C]Never a [Gbm/Db]sickness [Gm/D]that He cannot [Dm]heal;
[Gm/D]Moment [F/C]by moment, [C7/Bb]in woe [Am]or in [C7/Bb]weal,
[F/C]Jesus, my [C7/Bb]Savior, abides [Dm/A]with [Dbm/Ab]me still.
{end_of_verse}
